From: Francesco Stimola
 <1268108-francesco-stimola@users.noreply.gitlab.freedesktop.org>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 14:43:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] nouveau: give vp3 decoders progressive video buffers

VP3 to VP5 only had interlaced video buffers, which the VA frontend can
neither export nor derive images from, so players fall back to software
decoding.

PPP can write a whole frame too: bit 4 of its mode method selects field
output. Clear it for progressive targets, which are single-layer,
full-height buffers.

