Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 14:45:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] nouveau: give vp2 decoders progressive video buffers

VP2 only had interlaced video buffers, which the VA frontend can neither
export nor derive images from.

A progressive buffer now keeps an interlaced one, which VP decodes into
and reads as a reference. After each picture the decoder weaves its
fields into the progressive buffer, with a NIR fragment shader in the
nv50 3D blitter. Not tested on VP2 hardware.

